<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1526">1526</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad was a sultan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walashma-dynasty">Walashma dynasty</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a> in the early sixteenth century. During the ascendancy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-ibn-ibrahim-al-ghazi">Imam Ahmad</a> ibn Ibrahim al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazi">Ghazi</a>, he was kept on the throne as a nominal figurehead while real power lay with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a>. He was later succeeded in that role by his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umar-din">Umar Din</a>.</p></div>
